                    fb_round4_pooled:     `Reporting pooled OLS in the final round, after four hours of analysis, is the worst possible audit trail. Switch to TWFE with clustered SE.`,
                    fb_round4_fe_one:     `One-way FE in Round 4 leaves year shocks on the table. Two-way FE is the right baseline for the final memo.`,
                    fb_round4_fe_two:     `Two-way FE is the right baseline. Now lock down the inference and the robustness story.`,

                    fb_re_general:        `RE is more efficient than FE — but only when α_i is uncorrelated with regressors. Here it is not. Run the Hausman test before reporting RE.`,
                    fb_clustered_good:    `Cluster-robust SE at firm level: the point estimate is unchanged at +4.2% but the SE roughly tripled to 0.038. Result is no longer significant at conventional levels (t ≈ 1.1, p = 0.27). That is the honest report — Bertrand-Duflo-Mullainathan (2004 QJE) showed conventional SEs are typically too tight by 2–5× in serially correlated panels.`,
                    fb_unclustered_warning: `Reporting unclustered SE in a serially correlated panel in 2026 is a referee-grade error. Re-run with vce(cluster firm_id). Your t will fall from ~3.0 to ~1.1.`,
                    fb_hausman:           `Hausman test computed: H = 38.6, p < 0.001. RE is rejected — α_i is correlated with training_it. Report FE.`,
